[232.121539, "i", "cat <<EOF > /home/github/build/failed/failed_reasons.txt\nStep 1: Analysis of Build Errors\n\n1. ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'langchain.callbacks'\n   - Cause: The codebase was using an outdated import path for Langchain callback handlers. In newer versions of Langchain, these have moved to 'langchain_core.callbacks.base'.\n   - Fix: Updated the import in 'agentops/langchain_callback_handler.py'.\n\n2. AssertionError in tests/test_events.py: TestEvents.test_record_timestamp\n   - Cause: The 'record' method in 'Client' was returning early if no session was active, before updating the 'end_timestamp' of the event. In a test environment where the singleton 'Client' might have its session ended by a previous test, this caused the timestamp check to fail.\n   - Fix: Moved the 'end_timestamp' update logic before the session check in 'agentops/client.py'.\n\nStep 2: Proposed Changes\n\n- Patch 1: Fix Langchain import in 'agentops/langchain_callback_handler.py'.\n- Patch 2: Ensure 'end_timestamp' is updated in 'Client.rec"]
[232.12158, "i", "ord()' even if no session is active.\n\nStep 3: Apply Changes\n- Applied the fixes and verified with pytest. All 10 tests passed.\nEOF\n"]
